<p>A video is layers that arrive, stay and leave. These are the layers: each one a class on an element inside an <code>im-studio</code> frame, each drawn from the same tokens as the site, each with an <strong>in</strong>, a <strong>time</strong> and an <strong>out</strong>. Put a few in a frame and it is a shot; put shots in a sequence with a cut between them and it is a film. The docs show each at 960 × 540, live; the <a href="/content-creation/elements/scenes/">scenes</a> show them assembled at 1920 × 1080.</p>

