<h2>One clock</h2>
<p>Every element reads the same two times: <code>--im-studio-in-at</code> and <code>--im-studio-out-at</code>, in seconds from the start of the frame. They are the one place a frame carries a <code>style</code> attribute, because a time is data. The durations are the motion tokens, the curves are the motion tokens, so a cut in a video and a hover on the page have one feel — and <code>assets/im-motion.json</code> publishes the same numbers for an editor that is not a browser.</p>
